pkg:Evidence_v1_3_0 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.3.0 (MINOR release)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "MINOR: adds a BRSF-governed backlog (00-backlog/code_abundance_backlog_register_v1_0_0.ttl) replacing the ad-hoc plan the user asked to avoid for Path B (adopting RDODI v1.3.0's new default interactive-page pattern). Built the full 5-stage lineage ceremony from backlog-roadmap-framework's LINEAGE_OPERATING_DISCIPLINE_v5_0_0.md: Mission -> Scope -> Goal -> Objective -> Backlog, each stage closing in its own separately-pushed git commit per G18 (order witnessed by the remote, not claimed). Level declared L2_EvidenceBound (target L3_Governed, review 2026-11-25), granularity Epic (stated as the coarsest ordinary choice per G1), deployment PlanningEvent->Iteration->DeploymentUnit mapped onto this package's existing git-tag-per-release pattern. One Epic (EPIC-1) decomposed into 4 Stories before planning, per G3: corpus-contract authoring, quiz/glossary content, instantiate-and-verify, and Stage3-to-Stage4 section-count sync (the path-independent gap the fit-gap analysis identified). Both real checks pass: backlog_pipeline_verify_v1_0_0.py (order; all 5 stage digests reproduce from the finished register) and backlog_validate_v1_4_0.py at the declared level (0 sh:Violation, 44 sh:Warning -- legitimate disclosures, not defects). Reaching 0 violations took 3 rounds of fixing against the shapes file's exact SPARQL text rather than the TBox's prose, including one real bug found and fixed: several property values carried @en language tags, making them rdf:langString where the shapes require plain xsd:string."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "c244a4731ccad34cbaa877d2cd23cc2ff9b5e808f8fac71aab64c83564508587"^^xsd:string .
